  "description": "Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W (RP2350 + CYW43439), 21 x 51 mm. Top view, micro-USB at the TOP short edge, the antenna at the bottom edge. Two 1x20 0.1 in rows (through-hole + castellated) 17.78 mm (0.7 in) apart: pins 1-20 (GP0..GP15) down the left edge, pins 40..21 (VBUS..GP16) down the right edge, so the part straddles a breadboard centre channel. The 3-pin SWD debug header (SWCLK, GND, SWDIO) sits mid-board above the wireless module. Connector names are the pinout names (GP0, GND, VSYS ...); the physical pin number is in each description. The seven GND pins and the debug GND are one bus; AGND is a separate analogue ground and is NOT on the bus.",
  "sources": [
    "https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/picow/pico-2-w-datasheet.pdf",
    "https://www.raspberrypi.com/documentation/microcontrollers/pico-series.html"
